INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S QUARTERS - NIGHT

Storm outside. Sea slamming rock. A kerosene lamp. A shortwave radio on the table, buzzing.

HELGA STRAND (60s, oilskin, iron-gray braid) stands at the stove. Stirring. Not looking up.

At the table: her son, ARNE STRAND (30s, damp wool sweater, a bandage across one hand). He stares at the radio.

Their daughter-in-law, MAREN STRAND (30s, pregnant, hands wrapped around a cup) watches Arne watch the radio.

On the stairs, listening: THEO STRAND (10, pajamas, bare feet). He has been told to sleep.

By the window: CAPTAIN BASIL YEBOAH-KARLSSON (50s, drenched, sou'wester in hand). A stranger. Dripping onto the floorboards.

The radio hisses.

RADIO (V.O.)
(distorted)
Coast Guard to lighthouse. Come in.

Nobody moves.

Helga stirs.

RADIO (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Coast Guard to lighthouse. We have your vessel's mayday. Repeat. Come in.

Arne rises. Chair scrapes. Maren catches his wrist.

MAREN
Don't.

ARNE
Maren.

MAREN
You say one word to them and it's over.

ARNE
It's already over.

Helga sets the spoon down. Turns.

HELGA
Sit.

Arne sits. Maren lets go.

Basil steps from the window. Water pooling around his boots.

BASIL
They'll keep calling.

HELGA
Let them.

BASIL
My crew is in that water.

HELGA
Your crew is dead, Captain.

Silence. The radio crackles.

RADIO (V.O.)
Lighthouse. Acknowledge. Over.

Theo sits on the bottom stair. Pulls his knees up.

THEO
Daddy?

ARNE
Go to bed.

THEO
Who's talking?

MAREN
The radio, love. Go on.

Theo doesn't go.

Basil crosses the room in three strides and picks up the microphone. Arne is up again. Helga steps between them. The three of them stand locked, a breath apart, Maren half-risen behind with one hand on her belly, Theo gripping the banister.

BASIL
Let me answer.

HELGA
Put it down.

BASIL
They'll send a boat.

ARNE
They'll send a boat for us.

BASIL
For all of us.

HELGA
(quiet)
For him.

She nods at Arne. Basil looks. Looks at the bandage. At the rope burn climbing the wrist.

BASIL
(slowly)
You cut the line.

Arne says nothing.

BASIL (CONT'D)
You cut our line.

ARNE
The reef would have taken the lighthouse.

BASIL
The reef took forty men!

ARNE
(shouting)
I was trying to save my family!

Maren covers her mouth. Theo starts to cry without sound.

RADIO (V.O.)
Lighthouse, we have a visual on your lamp. Repeat, we have a visual. Hold position.

Basil lets the microphone drop. It swings on its cord, clicking against the table leg.

Helga takes it. Presses the key.

HELGA
(into the microphone)
This is Helga Strand. Lighthouse is secure.

A pause. Static.

RADIO (V.O.)
Copy, ma'am. Any survivors?

Everyone looks at Basil.

Basil stares at the floor. At the pool of seawater spreading around his boots. At the small bare feet on the stairs. He looks up.

BASIL
(barely)
One.

Helga lowers the microphone. Arne puts his face in his bandaged hand. Maren crosses to him and doesn't touch him.

Wind hits the tower. The lamp above them sweeps its beam across the window, turning, turning, turning.
